  "content": "{\"rationale\":\"GDN decode is a single-timestep update, so simplify_recurrence removes the unrolled time loop and its overhead. State is 8 heads of 128x128 with 128-wide reductions; a fused Triton kernel keeps the g/beta scaling, rank-1 update, and query projection in registers to avoid extra passes over FP32 state. rows=4 yields enough programs to fill V100's 80 SMs across the mostly small 54 workloads while limiting register pressure, and 4 warps (128 lanes) cleanly cover the 128-column reduction for good occupancy at low latency.\",\"implementation\":\"fused_triton\",\"rows\":4,\"warps\":4,\"simplify_recurrence\":true}"
}